%!PS-Adobe-3.0
%%Title: Watercolor spike -- bare opaque base for Approach C (issue #46)
%%BoundingBox: 0 0 620 620
%%EndComments

% The plainest possible render of the shared scene: three flat,
% opaque, unblended circles, no grain, no brush edges. Approach C
% starts from this (not from Approach A's already-finished render)
% because the point of the raster post-pass is to show what it alone
% adds -- diffusion-like bleed and paper grain -- on top of the
% cheapest possible vector base, the same way Approach B's alpha test
% isolates just the compositing mechanism rather than reusing
% Approach A's finishing touches.

(lib/artkit.ps) run
(docs/watercolor_prototypes/common_gesture.ps) run

1 1 1 setrgbcolor
0 0 620 620 rectfill

Circ1 circpath Color1 setcolor fill
Circ2 circpath Color2 setcolor fill
Circ3 circpath Color3 setcolor fill

showpage
